issues.suggestion:
Replace Math.random() with crypto.randomUUID() for secure ID generation:

function generateId(): string {
  return crypto.randomUUID();
}

Or if a custom format is required:

import { randomBytes } from 'crypto';

function generateId(): string {
  return `user_${Date.now()}_${randomBytes(5).toString('hex')}`;
}

Use a simpler regex or a well-tested library:

export function isValidEmail(email: string): boolean {
  // Simpler pattern less prone to ReDoS
  const emailRegex = /^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$/;
  return emailRegex.test(email);
}

Or better, use a library like validator.js:

import validator from 'validator';

export function isValidEmail(email: string): boolean {
  return validator.isEmail(email);
}

Use a battle-tested sanitization library like DOMPurify or validator.js:

import DOMPurify from 'isomorphic-dompurify';

export function sanitizeInput(input: string): string {
  return DOMPurify.sanitize(input, { ALLOWED_TAGS: [] });
}

Or if you only need basic text escaping:

import validator from 'validator';

export function sanitizeInput(input: string): string {
  return validator.escape(input);
}

Add explicit type, length and format checks:

if (typeof input.email !== 'string' || !input.email.trim()) {
  throw new Error('Email is required');
}
if (typeof input.name !== 'string' || !input.name.trim()) {
  throw new Error('Name is required');
}
if (input.email.length > 254) {
  throw new Error('Email is too long');
}
if (input.name.length > 100) {
  throw new Error('Name is too long');
}

Ensure email validation happens before transformation and add trim():

const normalizedEmail = input.email.trim().toLowerCase();
if (!isValidEmail(normalizedEmail)) {
  throw new Error('Invalid email format');
}

const user: User = {
  id: generateId(),
  email: normalizedEmail,
  name: sanitizedName,
  createdAt: new Date()
};

Add explicit error handling with context:

try {
  await saveUser(user);
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Failed to save user:', { email: user.email, error });
  throw new Error('Failed to create user: ' + (error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unknown error'));
}

return user;

